<!--
  The tests of the window (../../AppViews): of what it shows and what a click does,
  and pictures of it.

    LibraryModelTests   what the window shows and what a click does, with nothing drawn:
                        the model on a made-up PC
    EarlierVersionsTests
                        earlier versions in the window, and All Copies, with nothing
                        drawn: the mark, looking at a copy, putting one back, taking
                        that back
    ChordProModelTests  the ChordPro editor as far as it is the model's: what is done
                        with what is typed, and when it is saved; the two keys; Revert
    ChordProTypingTests the text box itself, typed into a key at a time; the letters
                        drawn behind it; the song's pane; and the box's undo with no box
    Typist              someone at that box: how a test types with no keyboard
    WindowListsTests    the two lists as far as they are numbers and words; the small
                        pictures before names; the look; what a row is called to a
                        screen reader
    PictureTests        pictures of the window, to be looked at
    MadeUpPC            what they stand on: a ProPresenter folder of copies of the test
                        files, in a temporary folder
    Pictures            drawing a view into a picture file; and a thread of the kind a
                        window has, for a test to work on

  THE PICTURES. An agent cannot look at a window; it can look at a picture file. So
  some of these tests draw a view into a PNG, and whoever changed how something is
  drawn opens the pictures and looks at them (spec/10-platforms.md, "Seeing what you
  have drawn"). Pictures.cs says where they go and how they are drawn. They do not go
  in the repository.

  Nothing here asks this PC's ProPresenter anything, reads a real library, or writes
  outside a folder of its own under the system's temporary folder (AGENTS.md, "The
  person's files").

  It is an .exe because xUnit, from its third version, makes every project of tests a
  program that can run itself. `dotnet test` runs it.
-->
<Project Sdk="Microsoft.NET.Sdk">
  <PropertyGroup>
    <TargetFramework>net10.0-windows</TargetFramework>
    <AssemblyName>Pro7ChordEditor.AppViews.Tests</AssemblyName>
    <RootNamespace>Pro7ChordEditor.AppViews.Tests</RootNamespace>
    <UseWPF>true</UseWPF>
    <OutputType>Exe</OutputType>
  </PropertyGroup>
  <ItemGroup>
    <PackageReference Include="xunit.v3" />
  </ItemGroup>
  <ItemGroup>
    <ProjectReference Include="..\..\AppViews\AppViews.csproj" />
    <ProjectReference Include="..\..\Song\Song.csproj" />
    <ProjectReference Include="..\TestData\TestData.csproj" />
  </ItemGroup>
</Project>
